After work, I go to the supermarket.
The supermarket is not far from my flat.
I need vegetables and pasta for my dinner.
First, I go to the vegetables.
I take tomatoes and carrots.
I also need fruit.
I put five apples into my basket.
Then I look for the pasta.
I find the pasta and go to the checkout.
The cashier is friendly.
"Hello!"
"That is twelve euros and fifty cents, please," she says.
"Here you go," I say and pay.
"Do you need the receipt?" she asks.
"No, thank you."
"Have a nice evening!" I answer.
"Thanks, you too," says the cashier.
I pack my food carefully into the shopping bag.
I have the laptop in my backpack.
The food and the laptop are well separated.
This way, the laptop stays safe.
I take the shopping bag and walk home.
